{"seq":34,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24869"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-004, category 1; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Engineering and Inventions] What ancient device is known as the world’s first computer?\nA. The Abacus\nB. The Antikythera Mechanism\nC. The Astrolabe\nAnswer: B. The Antikythera Mechanism, an ancient Greek device, is considered the world’s first computer for its sophisticated use of gears to predict astronomical positions.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-004.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"Which ancient Greek geared device, used to predict astronomical positions, is known as the world's oldest known (analogue) computer?"},{"field":"de","new":"Welches antike griechische Zahnradgerät zur Vorhersage astronomischer Positionen gilt als ältester bekannter (Analog-)Computer der Welt?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-004","category":1}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Engineering and Inventions] What ancient device is known as the world’s first computer?\nA. The Abacus\nB. The Antikythera Mechanism\nC. The Astrolabe\nAnswer: B. The Antikythera Mechanism, an ancient Greek device, is considered the world’s first computer for its sophisticated use of gears to predict astronomical positions."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f00840"}],"hash":"239b739f7e73"},
